@tradition midnight-toast
// Round 2: after tap night Greta Garcia makes toast for the night shift going on and the night owls. Every 4 weeks from week 4 (Days 26, 54...).
// Rules: FX24 (0.93.2, behind TRAD_0932_ON in section 13). Words: CS1 (plans/trad-0932-words.txt, claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300).
k: 1305
title: Midnight toast
when: every 4 weeks friday week 4
at: 23:00-23:30
min: 20
to-bed: yes
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: 1
who: garcia-greta always, night-owl 50%, night-shift 40%, everyone 5%
anim: garcia-greta talk, everyone drink
host: garcia-greta
from: garcia-greta
invite: host=garcia-greta odds=25% line="Midnight toast in the mess. For the night lot, and anyone else still up."

== mail
- Midnight toast tomorrow, {time}, the mess. Toast, butter, jam, a pot of tea, for the night shift going on and the owls still up. Pyjamas don't count against you.

== ask
- Midnight toast in the mess. Greta's making it. She says she isn't, but she is.   #funny
- Still up? There's toast in the mess. Night shift's treat.
- Toast at eleven. The best kind of late.

== here
- Butter's soft. Jam's from jar day.
- Another slice? Go on. Nobody's counting.   #warm
- Quiet in here this late. Nice.
- Tea's stewed. That's how the night shift likes it.   #funny

== thanks
- Greta makes toast and tea for the night shift going on and anyone still awake. The mess is quiet and warm.   #warm

== chatter
- Midnight toast last night. Best toast I've had aboard. Possibly because it was midnight.   #funny
- Greta says she only makes the toast for the night shift. She made me two slices.   #warm
- I went to bed full of toast. No regrets.   #funny
